User explicitly requests add bug and fold into active batch. During initial map processing CLI appears idle. Show one updating terminal progress line with current stage/work item, elapsed time, measured completed/total and ETA when estimable. Clear/remove it before final output. Decision: progress on interactive stderr only, never stdout; suppress redirected stderr, respect dumb terminals, avoid ANSI when unsupported, throttled updates, reliable cleanup on success/failure. ETA must be honest: unknown during unmeasurable parse stages, estimated for measured removal trials. Instrument actual stages and expensive contribution trials without changing comparison results, preserving all console/JSON/HTML/MD/PNG/WebP stream contracts. Verify using real maps and pseudo-terminal, capture stages then line removal; tests for redirects, failures, throttling, ETA bounds. Included implementation now, unlike backlog-only B060/B061. Serial shared CLI/DiffMode integration with image exports; independent core trial progress callback/helper work may run in parallel. Complete before final B044/B045/B046.